# SD
1. Customer is a physical and environmental object.
2. Manager is a physical and systemic object.
3. Sales Assistant is a physical and systemic object.
4. Lead is an informatical and systemic object.
5. Lead can be interested, not interested, open or selected.
6. State open is initial.
7. Sales Lead Handling is an informatical and systemic process.
8. Customer, Manager, and Sales Assistant handle Sales Lead Handling.
9. Sales Lead Handling affects Lead.
# SD1
1. Sales Lead Handling from SD zooms in SD1 into Lead Checking, Lead Selecting, Customer Calling, Note Sending, and Lead Processing, which occur in that time sequence, as well as Note.
2. Manager is a physical and systemic object.
3. Lead is an informatical and systemic object.
4. Lead can be interested, not interested, open or selected.
5. State open is initial.
6. Customer is a physical and environmental object.
7. Sales Assistant is a physical and systemic object.
8. Note is an informatical and systemic object.
9. Sales Lead Handling is an informatical and systemic process.
10. Lead Checking is an informatical and systemic process.
11. Manager handles Lead Checking.
12. Lead Checking affects Lead.
13. Lead Selecting is an informatical and systemic process.
14. Lead Selecting changes Lead from open to selected.
15. Manager handles Lead Selecting.
16. Customer Calling is an informatical and systemic process.
17. Customer and Sales Assistant handle Customer Calling.
18. Note Sending is an informatical and systemic process.
19. Sales Assistant handles Note Sending.
20. Note Sending occurs if Lead is at state interested, otherwise Note Sending is skipped.
21. Note Sending yields Note.
22. Lead Processing is an informatical and systemic process.
23. Manager handles Lead Processing.
24. Note initiates Lead Processing, which requires Note.
25. Lead Processing affects Lead.
26. Customer Calling changes Lead from selected to exactly one of interested or not interested.
